# API Client Patterns

## PredictionsApiClient Usage
The [PredictionsApiClient.cs](mdc:PetHoroscopeGenerator.Web/PredictionsApiClient.cs) handles AI predictions with these patterns:

## Service Registration
- Register in [Program.cs](mdc:PetHoroscopeGenerator.Web/Program.cs) with HttpClient
- Use service discovery with `https+http://` URLs
- Configure with Azure Key Vault for secrets

## Prediction Types
Use the `PredictionType` enum:
- `PredictionType.Pet` - Regular pet horoscopes
- `PredictionType.Plant` - Plant horoscopes  
- `PredictionType.Mythical` - Mythical creature horoscopes

## Caching Strategy
- 30-minute cache for predictions using `IMemoryCache`
- Cache key format: `{type}_{description}_{previewURL}`
- Check cache before making API calls

## Error Handling
- Return user-friendly messages for errors
- Handle authentication with `IHttpContextAccessor`
- Graceful fallback for missing configuration

## Usage Pattern:
```csharp
@inject PredictionsApiClient PredictionApi

private async Task Submit()
{
    crystalBallMessage = await PredictionApi.GetPredictionAsync(
        Text, previewUrl, PredictionType.Mythical);
}
```

## Configuration
- Azure OpenAI endpoint from `AZURE-OPENAI-ENDPOINT`
- Deployment name from `AZURE-OPENAI-GPT-NAME`
- API key from `AZURE-OPENAI-KEY`